# =============================================================================
# .gitignore for DADA2 16S Workflow
# =============================================================================

# =============================================================================
# R and RStudio
# =============================================================================
# History files
.Rhistory
.Rapp.history

# Session Data files
.RData
*.RData

# User-specific files
.Ruserdata

# RStudio files
.Rproj.user/
*.Rproj.user

# R Environment Variables
.Renviron

# =============================================================================
# Output Files (regenerated by pipeline)
# =============================================================================
# Results directory -- excluded in full. All pipeline outputs (ASV/taxonomy
# tables, phyloseq objects, Excel summaries, PDFs, and interactive HTML
# reports/barplots under results/**) are regenerated by re-running the
# notebooks, so none of it needs to be version-controlled; this also keeps
# the repository well clear of GitHub's 100 MB per-file push limit (this
# project's results/5_dada2_pipeline/checkpoints/*.RData files alone run
# ~110-114 MB each). The more targeted results/**/*.fastq, *.xlsx, *.csv
# patterns below are now redundant now that the whole directory is ignored,
# but are left in place as harmless documentation of what used to be
# excluded piecemeal before this project settled on excluding results/
# outright.
results/

# Checkpoint files
**/checkpoints/

# Console output logs
**/console_output/

# =============================================================================
# Large Data Files
# =============================================================================
# Ignore all raw FASTQ datasets. Users supply their own reads locally; no
# sequencing dataset is included in version control.
data/fastq/*.fastq
data/fastq/*.fastq.gz
data/fastq/*.fq
data/fastq/*.fq.gz

# Intermediate FASTQ files
results/**/*.fastq
results/**/*.fastq.gz

# =============================================================================
# Tool Binaries and Environments
# =============================================================================
# The entire tools/ directory -- excluded. Everything under it (Cutadapt and
# MultiQC's Python virtual environments, the FastQC release, the compiled
# FastTree binary, and the downloaded SILVA/GTDB reference databases in
# tools/trainsets/) is generated locally by the setup scripts in
# setup/, not authored in this repository, and is collectively
# well over 1 GB -- including several individual files (e.g. the MultiQC
# venv's kaleido executable and polars runtime .so files, and the SILVA
# assignTaxonomy trainset) that exceed GitHub's 100 MB per-file push limit
# on their own. A single directory-level pattern here supersedes the
# previous per-subfolder patterns, so nothing under tools/ is missed.
tools/

# Conda environments
*.conda
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# =============================================================================
# Temporary and Cache Files
# =============================================================================
# Temporary files
*.tmp
*.temp
*~
.~*

# macOS
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
._*

# Windows
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# Linux
*~
.fuse_hidden*
.directory
.Trash-*
.nfs*

# =============================================================================
# R Package Build
# =============================================================================
/*.tar.gz
/*.Rcheck/
.Rbuildignore
vignettes/*.html
vignettes/*.pdf
inst/doc

# =============================================================================
# Output Documents
# =============================================================================
# Notebook HTML reports are intentionally tracked alongside their .Rmd and
# manually generated .md companions so they can be viewed from GitHub.
R/notebooks/*_files/

# PDF outputs
*.pdf

# =============================================================================
# Excel and CSV outputs (regenerated)
# =============================================================================
results/**/*.xlsx
results/**/*.csv

# =============================================================================
# IDE and Editor Files
# =============================================================================
# VSCode
.vscode/
*.code-workspace

# Vim
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Emacs
*~
\#*\#
/.emacs.desktop
/.emacs.desktop.lock
*.elc

# Sublime Text
*.sublime-workspace
*.sublime-project

# =============================================================================
# Logs
# =============================================================================
*.log
logs/

# =============================================================================
# Archives
# =============================================================================
*.zip
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.rar
*.7z

# Note: this project previously kept an exception here
# (!results/2_fastqc_quality_reports/*.zip) to re-include FastQC's zip
# archives despite the general *.zip rule above. That exception is removed
# because it no longer has any effect: git does not descend into an
# already-excluded directory to test files against later negation patterns,
# and results/ is now excluded outright above. If you re-enable tracking of
# specific results/ files in the future, results/ itself must be
# un-excluded (or excluded with file-level patterns instead of a directory
# pattern) before a "!" exception underneath it can work again.

# =============================================================================
# Secrets and Credentials
# =============================================================================
.env
.env.local
*.pem
*.key
credentials/
secrets/
.positai
